# T1005 - what is vendored and what is tracked.
#
# The vendored BINARY payloads are downloaded and digest-verified by fetch-assets.sh.
# They are deliberately NOT committed: `typst` is 55.7 MB, the fonts are 0.8 MB, and
# a 55 MB binary in git is both unreviewable and unreproducible-by-inspection. Their
# integrity is guaranteed by the recorded SHA-256 values in LICENSES.md, which
# fetch-assets.sh enforces on every fetch, and by the container-side digest
# self-check the spike runs.
#
# This is also what keeps policy 10.1.5 / assertion V21 satisfiable: the vendored
# payloads are read-only binds, so `git status --porcelain backend/typst` stays empty
# across any number of render runs, and there is nothing in the repo a compile could
# write to.

# Pinned typst toolchain (fetch-assets.sh -> backend/typst/toolchain/).
# PIN and PIN.sha256 are NOT ignored: they are 96 bytes of text recording the pinned
# version and the binary digest, they are what makes the pin reviewable in a diff rather
# than only on the machine that ran the fetch, and they are the cheapest possible tripwire
# if the vendored binary is ever replaced. Everything else here is the upstream payload.
/toolchain/*
!/toolchain/.gitkeep
!/toolchain/PIN
!/toolchain/PIN.sha256

# Upstream release archives staged by fetch-assets.sh so the image build is hermetic
# (no egress at build time). Digest-pinned in LICENSES.md; never trusted unverified.
# The RECEIPT is 670 bytes of text listing every digest that was verified, so it IS
# tracked: it is the record of what the fetch actually checked, and it is diffable.
# The archives themselves (35 MB) are not.
/typst-dist/*
!/typst-dist/.gitkeep
!/typst-dist/RECEIPT

# Vendored, licence-recorded font set (fetch-assets.sh -> backend/typst/fonts/)
/fonts/*
!/fonts/.gitkeep

# Third-party Typst Universe packages, IF any are ever added. The spike vendors none;
# packages/clearance/ is first-party and tracked, because it is a few lines of
# reviewable source rather than a third-party payload.
/packages/preview/
/packages/thirdparty/
